.TH PATHCHORD 1 "November 2026" "PathChord" "PathChord manual"
.SH NAME
pathchordctl \- PathChord local management client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pathchord-ingressd
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B pathchord-egressd
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B pathchordctl
.RI [ global-options ]
.B status
.br
.B pathchordctl keygen --output
.I identity.json
.SH DESCRIPTION
PathChord provides local HTTP forwarding, HTTP CONNECT, SOCKS4/4a/5, and
same-port mixed listeners through the Ingress service.  The Egress service
accepts authenticated Path connections and forwards TCP and UDP targets.
Native packages install exactly one service role on a machine.  Each role
package includes only its dedicated daemon and the management client, and
conflicts with the opposite role package.  Both Unix profiles use the local
non-login pathchord account.  The
.B pathchordctl
client queries and mutates their local control endpoints.
.PP
Configuration is a directory of YAML, YML, or JSON resources.  Resources are
validated as one graph and are reloaded atomically.  Private identity and
credential files must be kept outside the configuration directory.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B pathchord-ingressd
Start the Ingress runtime.  Use
.B --config
for one resource file or
.B --config-dir
for a resource directory.
.TP
.B pathchord-egressd
Start the Egress runtime.  The Egress service owns its authorization database
and public Path listener.
.TP
.B pathchordctl status
Query the local control endpoint.
.TP
.B pathchordctl keygen
Create a new private static identity.  Existing output files are never
overwritten; the public key is printed to standard output.
.TP
.B pathchordctl enroll
Manage Egress authorization records from a protected local control endpoint.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI -c, --config\  path
Use one YAML, YML, or JSON resource file.
.TP
.BI -C, --config-dir\  path
Use a configuration directory.  Subdirectories are included.
.TP
.BI --identity\  path
Use the private identity file required by an enrolled topology.
.TP
.BI --data-dir\  path
Select the runtime cache and durable data directory for Ingress.
.TP
.BI --credentials-dir\  path
Select the directory containing private credential documents.
.TP
.BI --socket\  path
Select the local Unix socket or Windows Named Pipe used for control requests.
.TP
.BI --help
Show command-specific help.
.TP
.BI --version
Show the package version.
.SH CONFIGURATION SOURCES
Command-line options take precedence over environment variables.  When no
option is supplied, PATHCHORD_CONFIG or PATHCHORD_CONFIG_DIR is used.  The
account default is
.I ~/.config/pathchord/ingress
for regular Ingress users and
.I /etc/pathchord/ingress
for packaged Ingress services.  Egress uses the corresponding
.I ~/.config/pathchord/egress
or
.I /etc/pathchord/egress
source.  FreeBSD packages use the matching role directories under
.I /usr/local/etc/pathchord .
On Windows the corresponding service default is under the system profile;
packaged services pass an explicit configuration directory.
.PP
Set only one of PATHCHORD_CONFIG and PATHCHORD_CONFIG_DIR.  The two variables
cannot be combined, and a directory source does not have last-file-wins
semantics.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/pathchord/ingress/
Ingress system configuration directory on Linux and Alpine.
.TP
.I /etc/pathchord/egress/
Egress system configuration directory on Linux and Alpine.
.TP
.I /usr/local/etc/pathchord/ingress/
Ingress configuration directory on FreeBSD.
.TP
.I /usr/local/etc/pathchord/egress/
Egress configuration directory on FreeBSD.
.TP
.I /run/pathchord/ingress.sock
Ingress local control socket for root and service accounts on Unix.
.TP
.I /run/pathchord/egress.sock
Egress local control socket for root and service accounts on Unix.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/pathchord/
Regular-user Unix control sockets; if XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is absent, the sockets
are placed under ~/.config/pathchord/.
.TP
.I /var/run/pathchord/
FreeBSD runtime directory for the local control sockets.
.TP
.I %ProgramData%\\PathChord\\config\\ingress\\
Packaged Windows Ingress configuration directory.
.TP
.I %ProgramData%\\PathChord\\config\\egress\\
Packaged Windows Egress configuration directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
pathchord-ingressd --config-dir /etc/pathchord/ingress
pathchord-egressd --config-dir /etc/pathchord/egress
pathchordctl keygen --output /var/lib/pathchord-egress/egress.key.json
pathchordctl --socket /run/pathchord/egress.sock status
.EE
.SH SECURITY
Do not place private keys, bearer tokens, or credential values in a published
configuration template.  Restrict service data and control endpoints to the
service account and administrators.  Replace the loopback default before
exposing a listener to another network.
.SH PACKAGE LIFECYCLE
Upgrade and rollback preserve operator configuration, identities, credentials
and authorization data.  Uninstall the selected role explicitly before
installing another role; uninstall retains private state and the service
account.  Opposite-role installation is rejected before modifying the
installed service or private files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR rc.conf (5)
